[block
  'ORD-0037-schema-rust'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the measured proposal and the answers of the Regent'
    '.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-XSD.md, sections 4 and 5'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the first Order of the step, which writes the schema in both engines and validates in the JS'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/ORD-0036'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'step 1 of the trail to the final Explorer, its second Order: the Rust validates an XML against its schema as the JS does, so the oracle holds the gate in both engines'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'the answers of 2026-11-21: X4 a the engine validates with its own validator, the JS and the Rust each an Order; X6 a let us confirm the JS will leave correctly and the Rust will take over'
  [/ctx]
  [ins
    'validate in the Rust fromXML what the JS validates: what the schema declares and the content does not hold, what the content holds and the schema does not declare, a package with no schema, and a schema left empty before the gate, each by the same name and in the same order'
  [/ins]
  [ins
    'remove from the inverse oracle the set-aside that named the gate as JS-only'
  [/ins]
  [cnst
    'no hash of the snapshot moves: the gate changes what fromXML says, not what the engine emits'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'npm run check and npm run check:rust green'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the engines'
    'every fromXML the suite runs gives the same diagnostics in the Rust as in the JS, the gate included, with nothing set aside'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
  [cmp
    'the refusals'
    'a schema that drops a declaration and one that adds what the content lacks are each refused by name in the Rust fromXML, seen failing before they count'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
